late CNOOC from the broader risks of the energy transition or geopolitical tensions.  In the end, the conservative approach isn＊t about avoiding all risk〞it＊s about prioritizing long-term resilience over short-term gains. Selling CNOOC now allows the firm to reallocate capital to sectors with clearer growth trajectories and lower exposure to regulatory and market uncertainties. It＊s not just about protecting assets; it＊s about positioning the portfolio for the future, not the past.
